From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:25:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cellAudio: the host's own sounds added into every mixed block

A port that plays a sound of its own (Project Vekta's trophy notice) had to open a second audio device or stream,
which on Windows means a second WASAPI client, and its level and timing were apart from the game's.

Fix: ps3_audio_set_host_mix(fn). audio_mix_one_block calls fn(mix, frames, channels) on the mixing thread after
the title's ports are mixed and their lock is released, before the clip: the host adds its samples into the
interleaved float block at the output's channel count (front left and right first). Both backends (SDL and
WASAPI) and AUDIO_WAV get the same mix. fn must not block; NULL (the default) changes nothing.

ENHANCEMENT: the PS3 game has no host sounds. Seen in Level 1 (2026-11-26, Linux, SDL backend, stereo): the
trophy notice's sound found in the AUDIO_WAV capture of the mix at the moment the notice appeared (normalized
correlation 0.98 with the decoded asset at half amplitude).
---
 libs/audio/cellAudio.c | 7 +++++++
 libs/audio/cellAudio.h | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/audio/cellAudio.c b/libs/audio/cellAudio.c
index 5c5948b..10561db 100644
--- a/libs/audio/cellAudio.c
+++ b/libs/audio/cellAudio.c
@@ -464,6 +464,9 @@ static inline float ld_be_f32(const float* p)
     return f;
 }
 
+static volatile ps3_audio_host_mix_fn s_host_mix;
+void ps3_audio_set_host_mix(ps3_audio_host_mix_fn fn) { s_host_mix = fn; }
+
 /* Mix one block from all active ports into s_mix_buffer (stereo float) */
 static void audio_mix_one_block(void)
 {
@@ -606,6 +609,10 @@ static void audio_mix_one_block(void)
 
     mutex_unlock(&s_audio_mutex);
 
+    /* the host's own sounds (ps3_audio_set_host_mix), before the clip */
+    { const ps3_audio_host_mix_fn hm = s_host_mix;
+      if (hm) hm(s_mix_buffer, CELL_AUDIO_BLOCK_SAMPLES, s_out_ch); }
+
     /* Clip to [-1.0, 1.0] */
     for (u32 i = 0; i < CELL_AUDIO_BLOCK_SAMPLES * s_out_ch; i++) {
         if (s_mix_buffer[i] > 1.0f) s_mix_buffer[i] = 1.0f;
diff --git a/libs/audio/cellAudio.h b/libs/audio/cellAudio.h
index cef360a..3f3c01b 100644
--- a/libs/audio/cellAudio.h
+++ b/libs/audio/cellAudio.h
@@ -120,6 +120,11 @@ s32 cellAudioUnsetPersonalDevice(s32 iPersonalStream);
  * ps3_audio_clock_caught_up() is 1 once every block due has been mixed. */
 void ps3_audio_set_clock_ms(double ms);
 int  ps3_audio_clock_caught_up(void);
+/* The host's own sounds (ENHANCEMENT: a port's notice sound) added into every mixed block: fn(mix, frames, channels)
+ * on the mixing thread, after the title's ports and before the clip; mix is interleaved float at the output's channel
+ * count (front left and right first). It must not block. NULL turns it off. */
+typedef void (*ps3_audio_host_mix_fn)(float* mix, u32 frames, u32 channels);
+void ps3_audio_set_host_mix(ps3_audio_host_mix_fn fn);
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
